---
// The runtime database and one parameter container, step by step: FairTutorialDet2DigiPar of
// Tutorial2, as the macro create_digis.C uses it. Two drawings of the same stage: a wide one, and a
// tall one for narrow columns (container query on .rdb-box). The step classes go on the outer SVG.
//
// Facts (paths relative to the FairRoot repository):
// - examples/simulation/Tutorial2/macros/create_digis.C:59-68: io1 is a FairParRootFileIo (ROOT file,
//   opened "UPDATE"), parInput2 a FairParAsciiFileIo on parameters/tutdet.digi.par ("in");
//   setFirstInput(io1), setSecondInput(parInput2). :90-91: setOutput(io1), then saveOutput(). The output
//   is the same object as the first input. :81, :94: the order is fRun->Init(), saveOutput(), fRun->Run().
// - fairroot/parbase/FairRuntimeDb.h:33-37: containerList, firstInput ("first (prefered) input"),
//   secondInput ("used if not found in first input"), output. FairRuntimeDb.cxx:68: static contFactories.
// - Tutorial2/src/FairTutorialDet2Digitizer.cxx:23 fDigiPar(nullptr); :39-51 SetParContainers() calls
//   rtdb->getContainer("FairTutorialDet2DigiPar"), comment "parameters are not filled yet"; :53-63 ReInit()
//   gets the container again; :94-95 Init() only has the comment "now parameters are filled" (no read).
// - FairRuntimeDb.cxx:199-218 getContainer(): asks the factories in contFactories one after the other
//   until one returns a container. FairContFact.cxx:182-209 getContainer(): nullptr if the name is not in
//   its list; the existing container if containerList has it; else createContainer() and addContainer().
// - Tutorial2/src/FairTutorialDet2ContFact.cxx:15 static factory (FairContFact.cxx:157 adds it to the
//   list), :30 FairContainer "FairTutorialDet2DigiPar" (default context "TestDefaultContext", so no name
//   suffix, FairContFact.cxx:121-135), :47 new FairTutorialDet2DigiPar(...).
//   fairroot/base/sim/FairBaseContFact.cxx:24-37: FairBaseContFact (FairBaseParSet, FairGeoParSet) is the
//   other factory; libExSimulation2 links FairRoot::Base, so that factory registers first.
// - Tutorial2/src/FairTutorialDet2DigiPar.cxx:23 ftutdetdigiparstation(-1); :68-101 getParams() fills
//   "FairTutorialDet2DigiStations", "...SectorsPerStation", "FairTutorialDet2DigiPar".
//   parameters/tutdet.digi.par:10 [FairTutorialDet2DigiPar], :12 FairTutorialDet2DigiStations: Int_t 8.
// - fairroot/base/steer/FairRunAna.cxx:191 fRunId from the event header of the input, :201/209
//   SetParTask(), :220 initContainers(fRunId), :238 InitTask() (FairTask.cxx:49-88: SetParTask ->
//   SetParContainers, InitTask -> Init). With an input file, :198 calls initContainers(fRunId) once
//   before SetParTask(); FairTutorialDet2DigiPar is not in containerList then.
//   :568-584 CheckRunIdChanged(): new run ID -> Reinit(fRunId) (:589 initContainers) -> ReInitTask()
//   (not when the initialisation is static, :577).
// - FairRuntimeDb.cxx:464-484 initContainers(runId) (writes the old run first if the ID changes),
//   :508-564 readVersions() of both inputs, then init() of each container that is not static.
// - fairroot/parbase/FairParSet.cxx:55-76 init(): CallInitIO(firstInput); if true, done; else
//   CallInitIO(secondInput). :43-53 CallInitIO(): false for no input, else init(io) (warning if it fails).
//   FairParGenericSet.cxx:38-46 init(io) uses the "FairGenericParIo" of the input.
// - FairDetParRootFileIo.cxx:48-77, :111-130: the version comes from the FairRtdbRun of the run ID in the
//   ROOT file (FairParRootFileIo.cxx:71); no version -> false. :79-97 write(): Write(name), version = cycle.
// - FairGenericParAsciiFileIo.cxx:145 finds "[name]" (FairDetParAsciiFileIo.cxx:45-70), :261-270
//   getParams(), version 1, "initialized from Ascii file".
// - FairRuntimeDb.cxx:818-830 saveOutput(): writeContainers() (:317-339, calls writeContainer(), :385-462,
//   which writes a changed container) and writeVersions() (:303-315, runs->Write(): the versions of each
//   run ID). create_digis.C:88-89 also marks the container changed before saveOutput().
import Explainer from './Explainer.astro';

const steps = [
  {
    cap: 'The macro create_digis.C gives the runtime database two inputs. The first input is a ROOT file. The second input is the ASCII file tutdet.digi.par.',
    code: 'rtdb->setFirstInput(io1); rtdb->setSecondInput(parInput2);',
  },
  {
    cap: 'In SetParContainers(), the digitizer asks for its container by name. The runtime database asks the container factories, one after the other, until one knows the name.',
    code: 'rtdb->getContainer("FairTutorialDet2DigiPar")',
  },
  {
    cap: 'FairTutorialDet2ContFact creates the container and adds it to containerList. The digitizer keeps the pointer, but the parameters are not filled yet.',
    code: 'cont = createContainer(c);',
  },
  {
    cap: 'FairRunAna::Init() calls initContainers() with the run ID. The runtime database calls init() of each container in containerList.',
    code: 'fRtdb->initContainers(fRunId)',
    set: { run: 'run <runId>' },
  },
  {
    cap: 'init() reads from firstInput first. The ROOT file has no version of FairTutorialDet2DigiPar for this run ID, so the read returns false.',
    code: 'bool allFound = CallInitIO(rtdb->getFirstInput(), "first input");',
    set: { run: 'run <runId>' },
  },
  {
    cap: 'Then init() reads from secondInput. tutdet.digi.par has the section [FairTutorialDet2DigiPar], and getParams() fills the values from it.',
    code: 'allFound = CallInitIO(rtdb->getSecondInput(), "second input");',
    set: { run: 'run <runId>' },
  },
  {
    cap: 'Then FairRunAna::Init() calls Init() of each task. fDigiPar points to the filled container, so the task can use the values.',
    code: 'fTask->InitTask();',
    set: { run: 'run <runId>' },
  },
  {
    cap: 'saveOutput() writes the changed containers and the versions of the run to the output. Here the output is io1, so a later job finds the container in firstInput.',
    code: 'rtdb->setOutput(io1); rtdb->saveOutput();',
    set: { run: 'run <runId>' },
  },
  {
    cap: 'When the run ID changes in the event loop, FairRunAna calls initContainers() with the new ID. Then it calls ReInit() of each task.',
    code: 'Reinit(fRunId); fTask->ReInitTask();',
    set: { run: 'run <next runId>' },
  },
];
